  <h2>Accuracy and corrections</h2>
  <p>
    We correct errors of fact promptly and transparently. Corrections are appended to the article and
    can be requested at <a href="mailto:corrections@thecaravelgu.com">corrections@thecaravelgu.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Sourcing</h2>
  <p>
    Reporters identify themselves as writing for The Caravel. Anonymous sources are used only when
    necessary and with an editor's approval.
  </p>

  <h2>Independence and conflicts of interest</h2>
  <p>
    Writers disclose any personal, financial, or organizational interest relevant to their coverage.
    Members of an organization do not report on that organization.
  </p>

  <h2>Opinion and satire</h2>
  <p>
    Opinion and satire are clearly labeled and held to the same standard of factual accuracy as news
    reporting.
  </p>

  <h2>AI and generated content</h2>
  <p>
    Generative tools are not used to write articles. Any use for research or transcription is
    disclosed to editors.
  </p>

  <h2>Financial independence</h2>
  <p>
    The Caravel is student-owned and editorially independent. Advertising and sponsorship, if any,
    are disclosed and do not influence coverage.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
